  "implementation": [
    "Native partition copies the exact prefix buffer, assigns bounded paragraph source fields and rebases table/header/cell coordinates",
    "An optional local non-upstream block-split observer exposes only recognized partition metadata and borrowed buffers; separate from reference-definition callbacks",
    "Swift reconciles suffix coordinates against verified physical header fragments, including internal offsets and container indentation",
    "A complete-line prefix ends at its native-proven physical line boundary, avoiding another full prefix scan",
    "The native paragraph reference resolver is reused; definition-only prefixes are freed by native ownership rules and ordinary definitions populate the existing refmap",
    "Full original content remains available only through the split callback; afterward the native table retains only its header content",
    "No second Markdown grammar or document-source rewriting; every native change reverses to recorded original hashes"
  ],
